# Commit trace

When creating a git commit in this repo, include a [`docs/TRACE.md`](docs/TRACE.md) entry **in that same commit**. Do not commit code without it.

Add a new `##` entry at the top of TRACE (below the intro):

```markdown
## YYYY-MM-DD — commit subject
What: one or two lines, high level (not a file list)
Play: Playtesters | other Studio | skipped (MCP down) — one-line evidence
```

Keep the git subject as the existing 1–2 sentence **why**. TRACE is the in-repo journal; git log is not enough.

If Play did not run, write `Play: skipped — Studio MCP not connected` (or the real reason). Do not invent playtest evidence.
